mac_igmpproxy needs to be loaded before igmpproxy starts, for example
by adding the following line to /boot/loader.conf:

  mac_igmpproxy_load="YES"

Then make igmpproxy drop privileges by adding the following to
igmpproxy.conf:

  user igmpproxy
  chroot /var/empty

The policy applies to UID 422 (the igmpproxy user created by this
package) by default.  This can be changed with:

  sysctl security.mac.igmpproxy.uid=<uid>

and enforcement can be disabled with:

  sysctl security.mac.igmpproxy.enabled=0
